course: dictionary
lesson: 7907
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The dictionary lists them as 1), 2), 3), and so on. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning is right, so read the words before and after it. «After you stop, the heart rate falls fast in the first minute or two.» Here rate means how fast something happens, so heart rate is how fast your heart beats.
explain: «Frame rate is how many pictures a second a game shows.» Here rate means how much of one thing goes with one unit of another: pictures for each second. Ask yourself which meaning fits, then put it into the sentence to check that it makes sense.
explain: Rate can also be a price, as in «the hourly rate» for a job. And it can mean to judge how good something is: «I rate it 4 stars». Context is the key, because the same word can change its meaning from one sentence to the next.
fact: Rate can be a noun (rate, rates) or a verb (rate, rated, rating).
fact: «Rate» can mean how fast something happens, as in «heart rate» or «rate of growth».
fact: «Rate» can mean how much of one thing goes with one unit of another, such as 60 miles in each hour.
fact: «Rate» can mean a price or charge, such as «the hourly rate» for work.
fact: To rate something is to judge how good it is, as in «I rate it 4 stars»; «at any rate» means anyway.
exercise: «After you stop, the heart rate falls fast in the first minute or two.» In this sentence, what does rate mean? | A price or charge | Anyway | *How fast something happens | To judge how good something is
exercise: Maya says, «I rate it 4 stars.» What does rate mean here? | Anyway | A price or charge | *To judge how good something is | How fast something happens
exercise: «Frame rate is how many pictures a second a game shows.» What does frame rate measure? | The price of a game | *How many pictures for each second | The heart beating | How good a game is
test: «The hourly rate for the job is 10 pounds.» What does rate mean here? | Anyway | How fast something happens | *A price or charge | To judge how good something is
test: «At any rate, we can still go to the park.» What does at any rate mean? | Fast | Judged as good | *Anyway | Only at the park
exam: Ella says rate always means speed. Is she right? | Yes, and it is always a number | *No, rate has several meanings, so the context decides | No, rate is only a verb | Yes, rate only means speed
